.Dd $Mdocdate: August 7 2026 $
.Dt FUGUWEB 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm fuguweb
.Nd build a documentation website for a Perl project
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm fuguweb
.Op Fl hq
.Op Fl Fl project Ar dir
.Ar command
.Op Ar argument ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
builds one static website from the documentation that a Perl project
already keeps:
.Xr mdoc 7
manuals,
POD sidecars,
and Markdown.
There is no templating language and no JavaScript.
.Nm
runs
.Xr mandoc 1 ,
.Xr lowdown 1
and
.Xr pod2man 1 ,
and wraps each result in one shared chrome.
.Pp
.Nm
operates on a project:
a directory that has a
.Pa .fuguwebrc
file.
The
.Cm init
command writes one.
If you do not give
.Fl Fl project ,
.Nm
searches up from the current directory for a
.Pa .fuguwebrc
file.
The directory that holds this file is the project root.
.Pp
The build reads nothing from the network,
writes nothing outside the output directory,
and gives the same bytes for the same checkout.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl Fl project Ar dir
Use
.Ar dir
as the project root,
and do not search for it.
.It Fl q , Fl Fl quiet
Do not show informational output.
.It Fl h , Fl Fl help
Show the usage message.
.El
.Pp
These commands are available:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm init Op Ar dir
Write a starter
.Pa .fuguwebrc
in
.Ar dir
(default: the current directory).
The command refuses a directory that already has one.
.It Cm build Op Fl Fl out Ar dir
Render the whole site.
.Fl Fl out
overrides the
.Va out_dir
setting,
and a relative value is resolved against the project root,
exactly as the setting is.
.Pp
The build also removes a page that the site no longer holds,
so a manual that was renamed leaves nothing behind.
.Pp
The command checks the renderers first,
and names the one that is missing.
It then rejects a malformed manual source,
because such a page must fail the build and not render badly.
.It Cm clean Op Fl Fl out Ar dir
Remove the output directory.
.Pp
The command removes a built site and refuses anything else.
A build writes one flat directory of files,
so a target that holds a subdirectory,
a symlink,
or anything else that no build made is refused by name.
.Pp
Both
.Cm build
and
.Cm clean
also refuse the root of the filesystem,
the home directory,
the project root,
and any directory that holds the project.
.Pp
With
.Fl Fl out
the command needs no
.Pa .fuguwebrc ,
because the target is named on the command line.
.Cm clean
is the command you reach for when the description is the thing that is
broken.
.It Cm check Oo Fl Fl out Ar dir Oc Op Fl Fl verbose
Check a built site:
that every page and asset is there and is not empty,
that every page has a title and the whole navigation,
that every local link and every fragment resolves,
that no reference is root-absolute or a
.Ql file:
URL,
that no local link reads as a URL scheme,
that no manual cross-reference dangles,
that every page is reachable from the front page,
and that the output holds the site and nothing else.
.Pp
The command prints one line for each problem and exits 5.
It says nothing and exits 0 when the site is good.
.Fl Fl verbose
also notes every external link.
The command never fetches one:
the build and its checks touch no network.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "share/fuguweb/style.css" -compact
.It Pa .fuguwebrc
The site description, at the project root.
.It Pa share/fuguweb/style.css
The base stylesheet, which ships with the tool.
The
.Va stylesheet
setting overrides the search for it.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits with one of these values:
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width Ds -offset indent -compact
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
General error.
.It 2
Invalid arguments.
.It 3
Configuration error, or not in an
.Nm
project.
.It 4
A renderer failed.
.It 5
The check found a problem.
.It 6
A renderer is not installed.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Build the site and check it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ fuguweb build --out web/build
$ fuguweb check --out web/build
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr lowdown 1 ,
.Xr mandoc 1 ,
.Xr pod2man 1 ,
.Xr mdoc 7
.Pp
The module documentation is in the
.Pa .pod
sidecars beside
.Pa lib/App/FuguWeb/ .
